    ('D001', 'start_here', 'Understand Software Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Software engineering is the discipline of designing, building and testing computer programs and mobile applications. Practitioners write and debug code, analyse what a program should do, test software at different levels, and manage changes to systems, in roles such as software analyst, tester, mobile application developer and cloud engineer. They typically work in technology firms, banks, telecoms companies and government agencies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D001", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D001', 'build_next', 'develop and document software', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Software Engineering work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D001", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
