    ('D004', 'start_here', 'Understand Cybersecurity', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Cybersecurity is the practice of protecting computers, networks and information from attack. Day to day, professionals administer security settings, investigate digital evidence after incidents, respond to cyber attacks, test defences as ethical hackers and manage security risks. They work in banks, telecoms companies, government agencies and any organisation that runs computer systems.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D004", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
