    ('D006', 'start_here', 'Understand Internet of Things', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: The Internet of Things connects everyday devices such as sensors, meters and appliances to the internet so they can send and receive information. Specialists write the firmware inside these devices, design the networks that link them, plan complete solutions, secure them against attack, and test that everything works, documenting any faults. Manufacturers, telecoms companies and technology firms are typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D006", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
