    ('D007', 'start_here', 'Understand UI/UX Design', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: UI/UX design is about how websites and apps look, feel and respond when people use them. Designers plan screens and web pages, create graphics, illustrations and animation, follow client briefs, and test digital products for ease of use and accessibility. They work in design studios, technology firms, media houses and marketing departments.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D007", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
