    ('D008', 'start_here', 'Understand Telecommunications', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Telecommunications is the engineering behind phone calls, internet connections and data networks. Engineers design radio-frequency and signal systems, planners work out how much network capacity is needed, technicians install and maintain equipment, and managers direct projects, budgets and technical teams. Telecoms companies and government agencies are the usual employers, and practising engineers in Nigeria register with COREN.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D008", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
