    ('D139', 'start_here', 'Understand Game Design', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Game design covers the creation of video games and animated worlds. Illustrators, animators and 3D artists build models, characters and visual environments; programmers code game mechanics and player-facing features; and directors lead the artistic and technical vision of a production. Most roles are based in game and animation studios.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D139", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
