    ('D009', 'start_here', 'Understand Data Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Data science uses statistics and computer programming to draw useful conclusions from large collections of information. Some practitioners build data pipelines, artificial-intelligence models and software systems, while others model data with advanced mathematics, manage research information and write up findings in technical reports. Banks, telecoms companies, research bodies and government agencies all employ them.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D009", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
