    ('D011', 'start_here', 'Understand Quantitative Finance', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Quantitative finance applies mathematics, statistics and economics to financial markets. Some practitioners buy and sell shares, currencies and other assets as traders; others analyse investments, risk and market trends to guide decisions; a third group builds the mathematical models behind pricing and risk. They usually work in banks, investment firms, insurance companies and trading houses.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D011", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
