    ('D012', 'start_here', 'Understand FinTech Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: FinTech engineering builds the software that powers financial services such as payments, banking apps and blockchain systems. Developers write backend code, data engineers manage the information flowing through these systems, and testers run structured checks, record faults and document results so money-handling software works reliably. Banks, payment companies and technology firms employ these teams.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D012", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
