    ('D014', 'start_here', 'Understand Actuarial Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Actuarial science uses mathematics and statistics to measure risk, mainly for insurance and pensions. Actuaries model how likely future events are and what cover should cost, underwriters and rating analysts assess individual risks, and claims handlers process what policyholders are owed. Most work in insurance companies, consulting firms and banks, and full actuaries qualify through professional fellowship examinations.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D014", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
