    ('D015', 'start_here', 'Understand Accounting', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Accounting is the recording, checking and reporting of an organisation''s money. Accountants prepare and interpret financial statements, audit records, advise on tax, control budgets, and handle billing, payroll and back-office processing. They work in accounting firms, banks, government agencies and businesses of all sizes; in Nigeria the chartered route runs through bodies such as ICAN or ANAN.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D015", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D015', 'build_next', 'analyse complex business cases', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Accounting work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D015", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
