    ('D060', 'start_here', 'Understand Banking, Credit', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Keeping money safe and lending it out is the everyday business of banking and credit. Bank tellers and cashiers serve customers, credit analysts and advisers assess loans and mortgages, clerks handle settlements and foreign exchange records, and managers lead branches and credit unions. Banks, mortgage firms and credit unions are the natural workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D060", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
