    ('D061', 'start_here', 'Understand Insurance', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Insurance protects people and businesses against loss in exchange for regular payments. Underwriters assess risk and price cover, claims handlers and managers settle claims, brokers arrange policies for clients, fraud investigators check suspicious cases, and some specialists run pension schemes. Insurance companies and brokerages employ most of the profession.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D061", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
