    ('D062', 'start_here', 'Understand Trading', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Trading is the buying and selling of financial assets such as currencies, shares, commodities and energy. Traders deal on markets throughout the day, securities analysts study market trends and financial products, and investment managers and planners advise clients on funds and risk. Banks, investment firms and brokerages are the typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D062", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
