    ('D158', 'start_here', 'Understand Corporate Finance, Investment Banking', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Corporate finance and investment banking deal with how companies raise, invest and manage money. Securities and mergers analysts study company performance and financial statements, while controllers, budget analysts and bank managers oversee funds and financial processes. Banks, investment firms and large corporations are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D158", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
