    ('D016', 'start_here', 'Understand Electrical', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Electrical engineering deals with electricity, circuits and electronic devices. Engineers design power systems, batteries, sensors and electronics for products ranging from medical devices to satellites, while technicians test, calibrate and maintain electrical equipment and lines. Power companies, manufacturers, telecoms companies and construction firms employ them, and practising engineers in Nigeria register with COREN.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D016", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
