    ('D020', 'start_here', 'Understand Environmental Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Environmental engineering tackles pollution, waste and water quality. Technicians operate water, wastewater and waste treatment plants, engineers design solutions to pollution, climate and sustainability problems, and inspectors check that organisations comply with environmental, health and safety laws. Water utilities, waste management companies, mining firms and government agencies employ people in this field.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D020", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
