    ('D021', 'start_here', 'Understand Architecture', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Architecture is the design of buildings, interiors and the spaces around them. Architects draw up designs that satisfy building codes and regulations, urban and transport planners shape how cities and land are used, and site staff inspect, survey and support construction on the ground. Architectural practices, construction firms and government planning agencies are typical workplaces; Nigerian architects register with ARCON.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D021", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
