    ('D022', 'start_here', 'Understand Mining', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Mining is the finding and extraction of minerals, oil and gas from the earth. Geologists and engineers explore and plan extraction sites, crews operate rigs, drills and underground machinery, managers run mines, quarries and production sites, and specialists survey ground, test metals and enforce safety rules. Mining companies, oil and gas producers and quarrying firms are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D022", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
