    ('D069', 'start_here', 'Understand Aviation', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Aviation is the operation of aircraft and the systems that keep air travel safe. Pilots fly aeroplanes, helicopters and drones, air traffic controllers direct aircraft movements, technicians overhaul engines and service flight systems, and cabin crew look after passengers on board. Work is typically found with airlines, airports and civil aviation agencies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D069", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
