    ('D072', 'start_here', 'Understand Geospatial Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Geospatial science involves measuring, mapping and studying the Earth''s land, water and minerals. Surveyors take precise measurements of land, mines and seabeds for maps and property records, while geologists, hydrologists and oceanographers study rocks, groundwater and the sea using mathematics and geographic information systems. Typical employers include mining companies, construction firms and government agencies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D072", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
