    ('D074', 'start_here', 'Understand Occupational Health, Safety', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Occupational health and safety focuses on preventing accidents, illness and harmful conditions at work. Inspectors visit factories, building sites, food businesses and hospitals to check that health, hygiene and waste laws are being followed, carrying out audits and reporting hazards. Many are employed by government agencies, with others working for large industrial and transport companies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D074", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
