    ('D146', 'start_here', 'Understand Building Services Engineering — Mechanical, Electrical', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Building services engineering deals with the mechanical and electrical systems that make buildings work, such as lighting, air conditioning, fire protection and automation. Engineers in this field design these systems from drawings, maintain them, and increasingly connect them to smart controls. Construction firms and engineering consultancies are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D146", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
