    ('D147', 'build_next', 'Understand electronics', 'Build this after the orientation because strong CCMAS curriculum anchors show the concept is taught in programmes mapped to this domain.', 'CCMAS curriculum anchors: Engineering::ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING / Applied Electricity II; Engineering::ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING / Measurements and Instrumentations; Engineering::ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING / Power Electronics; Engineering::SYSTEMS ENGINEERING / Solid Modelling and Design', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 6, '{"source": "ccmas_programme_domain_evidence", "domain_id": "D147", "anchor": "electronics", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D147', 'build_next', 'Understand engineering principles', 'Build this after the orientation because strong CCMAS curriculum anchors show the concept is taught in programmes mapped to this domain.', 'CCMAS curriculum anchors: Engineering::CHEMICAL ENGINEERING / Chemical Product Design; Engineering::CHEMICAL ENGINEERING / Chemical Engineering Research Project RECOMMENDATION: TCH 555 – Chemical Engineering Research Project be taken/taught over the two semesters of the final year.; Engineering::PETROCHEMICAL ENGINEERING / Final Year Project; Engineering::PETROCHEMICAL ENGINEERING / Process Dynamics and control in Petrochemical plant Note: It is expected that 2hrs every week should be used by students to learn how to use modelling software such as MATLAB, POLYMATH, CHEMCAD, HYSYS, microsoft excel etc, for simple calculations based on the contents of these courses.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 7, '{"source": "ccmas_programme_domain_evidence", "domain_id": "D147", "anchor": "engineering principles", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
