    ('D156', 'start_here', 'Understand Land Surveying, Cadastral Mapping', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Land surveying and cadastral mapping measure land and record its boundaries. Surveyors take precise measurements on building sites, mines and waterways, while cartographers, photogrammetrists and geographic information systems specialists turn those measurements into maps and digital records. Government agencies, construction firms and mining companies rely on their work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D156", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D156', 'build_next', 'perform construction work to defined occupational standards', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Land Surveying, Cadastral Mapping work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D156", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
