    ('D023', 'start_here', 'Understand Medicine', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Medicine is the profession of diagnosing and treating illness. General practitioners and specialist doctors examine patients and decide on treatment, technical staff provide laboratory, audiology and prosthetic support, and managers run hospitals and clinical information systems. Hospitals, clinics and government health agencies are the main workplaces, and doctors in Nigeria must register with the Medical and Dental Council.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D023", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
