    ('D024', 'start_here', 'Understand Nursing', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Nursing centres on the day-to-day care of patients. Specialist nurses and advanced practitioners deliver nursing, mental-health and midwifery care, paramedics and ambulance crews respond to emergencies, and support workers assist with procedures, records and hands-on personal care. Most work in hospitals, clinics, maternity units and community health services, and Nigerian practice requires registration with the Nursing and Midwifery Council.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D024", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
