    ('D026', 'start_here', 'Understand Public Health', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Public health protects the health of whole communities rather than one patient at a time. Inspectors enforce food, workplace and community health standards, officers and physicians coordinate emergency responses and prevention work, and scientists track diseases and analyse health statistics. Government agencies, hospitals and international health organisations are typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D026", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
