    ('D027', 'start_here', 'Understand Biomedical', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Biomedical science studies living things, from microbes to the human body, mainly through laboratory work. Microbiologists, pharmacologists and physiologists research organisms, medicines and how bodies function, while technicians run laboratory tests and support biology and agricultural science. Hospitals, research institutes, universities and pharmaceutical companies employ them; medical laboratory scientists in Nigeria are licensed by MLSCN.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D027", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
