    ('D064', 'start_here', 'Understand Psychology, Counselling', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Psychology and counselling deal with how people think, feel and behave, and with helping them through personal difficulty. Educational and health psychologists assess and support clients, while counsellors work with problems such as addiction, marriage and family planning, using client-centred methods. Hospitals, schools, social service agencies and private practices are typical settings.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D064", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
