    ('D066', 'start_here', 'Understand Veterinary Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Veterinary science is the study and treatment of animal health and welfare. Veterinarians diagnose, treat and rehabilitate sick or injured animals, veterinary nurses assist with care and breeding procedures, and others provide animal therapy or study behaviour and nutrition. Practitioners work in veterinary clinics, on farms and for government agencies, and must register with the Veterinary Council of Nigeria to practise.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D066", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
