    ('D068', 'start_here', 'Understand Allied Health', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Allied health covers the healthcare professions that support diagnosis, treatment and recovery alongside doctors and nurses. Physiotherapists and occupational therapists help patients regain movement and daily skills, biomedical scientists analyse samples in laboratories, and radiographers produce medical images, supported by assistants and technicians. Hospitals, clinics, rehabilitation centres and sports organisations are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D068", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
