    ('D029', 'start_here', 'Understand Human Resources', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Human resources manages the people side of an organisation. Practitioners recruit staff, train and coach employees, analyse pay and benefits, handle labour relations under employment law, and guide careers, equality and inclusion programmes. HR roles exist wherever people are employed, from banks and manufacturers to government agencies, schools and charities.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D029", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
