    ('D033', 'start_here', 'Understand Product Management', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Product management is the work of guiding a product from idea to finished item and setting the direction a business takes with it. Product owners and development managers lead strategy, engineers and architects build the underlying technology, and analysts scope requirements, costs and processes. Most work in manufacturing companies, technology firms and other large businesses.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D033", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
