    ('D034', 'start_here', 'Understand Supply Chain Management', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Supply chain management is about moving goods from where they are made to where they are needed, at the right time and cost. People in this field schedule freight, ships, rail and cargo movements, run warehouses and distribution, handle customs and sourcing, and analyse logistics costs. Employers include shipping lines, airlines, ports, manufacturers and trading companies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D034", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
