    ('D035', 'start_here', 'Understand Logistics', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Logistics deals with the practical movement of goods and people by road, rail, air and sea. Some workers drive buses, trucks and forklifts; others load and dispatch goods in warehouses and docks, manage fleets and ports, or coordinate shipping, customs and forwarding. Transport companies, warehouses, ports and event organisers are typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D035", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
