    ('D036', 'start_here', 'Understand Procurement', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Procurement is the business of buying the goods and services an organisation needs to operate. Buyers identify suppliers, maintain supplier relationships and purchase goods or trade commodities, freight and imports, while analysts study costs and processes to improve purchasing decisions. Manufacturers, trading companies, wholesalers and government agencies employ most procurement staff.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D036", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
