    ('D076', 'start_here', 'Understand Maritime', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Maritime work covers life and labour at sea, from sailing and fishing to ship engineering and diving. Officers navigate and command vessels, deckhands and engine crew keep ships running, naval engineers design ships and marine structures, and divers work underwater on construction, harvesting and rescue. Shipping companies, ports, fishing fleets and offshore firms provide most of the work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D076", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
