    ('D079', 'start_here', 'Understand Customs, Trade', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Customs and trade is about moving goods and people legally across borders and through supply chains. Customs and immigration officers inspect cargo and clear travellers, while import-export specialists, forwarding managers and distribution managers organise shipping, warehousing and transport. Employers include government border agencies, shipping and logistics companies, and freight forwarding firms.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D079", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
