    ('D037', 'start_here', 'Understand Legal Practice', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Legal practice covers the making, interpretation and application of law. Lawyers and legal consultants advise clients and argue cases, judges and court clerks run court processes and enforce decisions, and legal assistants compile documents and carry out legal research. Typical workplaces include law firms, courts, companies and government agencies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D037", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
