    ('D038', 'start_here', 'Understand Compliance, Regulation', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Compliance and regulation work makes sure people and organisations follow laws, rules and government policy. Officers inspect goods and borders, enforce tax and safety rules, shape public policy and programmes, and manage contracts, procurement and regulatory affairs inside organisations. Government agencies, banks and large companies employ most of them.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D038", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
