    ('D149', 'start_here', 'Understand Diplomacy, International Relations', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Diplomacy and international relations manage a country''s dealings with other nations. Diplomats and ambassadors lead embassies and represent their nation abroad, while political affairs and intelligence officers handle foreign policy, trade, election observation and humanitarian issues. Ministries of foreign affairs, embassies and international organisations are the typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D149", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
