    ('D163', 'start_here', 'Understand Intellectual Property Law, Patents', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Intellectual property law protects inventions, brand names and creative works. Patent and trademark attorneys prepare applications, present legal arguments and protect their clients'' interests, while paralegals and administrators manage case files and paperwork. Most work is found in law firms, large companies and government registries, and practising as a lawyer requires being called to the Bar.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D163", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
