    ('D041', 'start_here', 'Understand Scientific Research', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Scientific research is the systematic study of the natural world through observation and experiment. Chemists, geologists and environmental scientists design studies and draft scientific papers, while technicians run laboratory tests, collect samples and support biology and agriculture research. Laboratories, research institutes, universities and government agencies are the usual workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D041", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
