    ('D043', 'start_here', 'Understand Journalism', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Journalism involves gathering information and turning it into accurate news and written content. Correspondents and vloggers report stories, presenters deliver them on air, and editors, fact checkers and translators check grammar, accuracy and editorial standards before publication. Newspapers, broadcasting stations, publishing houses and online media provide most of the work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D043", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
