    ('D065', 'start_here', 'Understand Translation, Interpretation', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Translation and interpretation is the work of converting speech and writing from one language into another so that people who speak different languages can understand each other. Translators work on written texts while interpreters convert speech in real time; others subtitle films, interpret sign language or compile dictionaries. Typical employers include courts, media houses, publishers and international organisations.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D065", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
