    ('D071', 'start_here', 'Understand Sports Management', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Sports management is about training athletes and running the organisations, venues and competitions around them. Coaches plan sessions and lead teams, performance analysts study matches, talent scouts identify promising players and referees officiate games, while academy and athletic directors manage clubs and facilities. Jobs are usually with sports clubs, academies, schools and government sports bodies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D071", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
