    ('D152', 'start_here', 'Understand Museum Curation, Cultural Heritage, Archives', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Museum curation, cultural heritage and archives work protects and organises a society''s art, objects and records. Curators plan collections and exhibitions, art restorers repair damaged works, and librarians and archivists manage information, from physical documents to digital archives. Museums, galleries, libraries and cultural institutions provide most of the work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D152", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
