    ('D153', 'start_here', 'Understand Music Production', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Music production is the craft of creating and recording music and sound. Sound engineers record, mix, edit and master audio for songs, media and games, while conductors, arrangers and music directors compose and lead performances. Recording studios, broadcasters and live event organisations are common workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D153", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
