    ('D045', 'start_here', 'Understand Public Administration', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Public administration is the running of government and public institutions. Civil registration officers, urban planners and policy officers develop policy and public programmes, inspectors enforce customs, tax and safety rules, and senior officials and ambassadors lead ministries and diplomacy. Nearly all work in government ministries, agencies, local councils and embassies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D045", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
