    ('D046', 'start_here', 'Understand Social Work', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Social work supports people facing difficulty, from children in care to families in crisis. Qualified social workers and counsellors guide individuals through problems such as family planning and recovery from violence, frontline workers support vulnerable adults and children in residential settings, and nannies and day-care workers mind children. Employers include government social services, care homes, charities and schools.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D046", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
