    ('D063', 'start_here', 'Understand Economics', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Economics studies how money, markets and government policy shape a society. Economists and researchers analyse statistics and market trends, while advisers and policy analysts guide decisions on tax, trade and economic development, often working closely with local representatives. Government ministries, research bodies and banks are common employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D063", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
