    ('D073', 'start_here', 'Understand Library, Archive', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Library and archive work is about organising, preserving and sharing information, records and cultural collections. Librarians and information managers help people find the material they need, curators plan exhibitions, and conservators and art handlers care for artefacts and digitise documents. Most posts are in libraries, museums, universities and government archives.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D073", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
