    ('D143', 'start_here', 'Understand Forensic Science, Digital Forensics', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Forensic science applies science and computing to the investigation of crime. Digital forensics experts and security specialists recover evidence from computers and respond to cyber attacks, laboratory technicians run biological analyses, detectives gather evidence, and pathologists examine medical evidence. Employers include police services, government agencies and security firms.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D143", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
