    ('D151', 'start_here', 'Understand Criminology, Criminal Justice', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Criminology and criminal justice cover the study of crime and the running of the justice system. Police officers and detectives investigate offences and handle evidence, prison officers guard and manage correctional facilities, and criminologists study why crime happens and supervise offender rehabilitation. Police services, prisons and government agencies are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D151", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
