    ('D047', 'start_here', 'Understand Agricultural Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: From crops to livestock, agricultural science combines farming practice with the study of plants, animals and the environment. Crop production managers, breeders and shepherds grow crops and raise animals, researchers study genetics, biology and aquaculture, and technicians supervise farm and fish sites. Farms, research institutes, agribusinesses and government agricultural agencies offer most positions.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D047", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
