    ('D049', 'start_here', 'Understand Automotive Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Automotive engineering is the design, testing and upkeep of vehicles and their systems. Engineers design engines, powertrains and mechanical systems, technicians test, inspect and maintain vehicles and machinery, and mechanics repair, restore and service cars and their components. Vehicle manufacturers, engineering workshops and transport companies are typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D049", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
