    ('D050', 'start_here', 'Understand Industrial Automation', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Industrial automation focuses on the machines and control systems that run modern factories. PLC programmers and automation engineers design automated machinery, instrumentation technicians keep control systems working, and assemblers and supervisors build equipment and run automated production lines. Manufacturing plants and engineering firms are the usual employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D050", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
