    ('D075', 'start_here', 'Understand Fashion, Textiles', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Fashion and textiles is the making of clothing, shoes, fabrics and accessories. Some workers cut, sew and craft garments by hand, others operate cutting, sewing, dyeing and finishing machines, and patternmakers and prototypers develop new designs, fabrics and products. Garment factories, textile mills, tailoring workshops and design studios are the typical workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D075", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
