    ('D052', 'start_here', 'Understand Construction Management', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Construction management is the planning and supervision of building work from start to finish. Quantity surveyors estimate costs, site managers and supervisors direct trades and enforce safety on site, bricklayers and plumbers carry out the building work, and engineers handle roads, water and structures. Construction firms, engineering companies and government agencies run most projects.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D052", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
