    ('D053', 'start_here', 'Understand Hospitality', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Hospitality is the service of looking after guests in hotels, restaurants and tourism. Receptionists and concierges welcome visitors, chefs lead kitchens, waiters and guides serve guests directly, and managers run hotels, events and tour operations while handling budgets and complaints. Hotels, restaurants, resorts and event companies provide the work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D053", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
