    ('D054', 'start_here', 'Understand Oil', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Finding petroleum underground and turning it into usable products is the focus of oil and gas work. Petroleum geologists and drilling engineers study rock and plan wells, operators run drills, pumps and refinery control rooms, and managers oversee offshore installations and production. Oil companies, refineries and servicing firms are the principal employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D054", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
