    ('D055', 'start_here', 'Understand Chemical Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Chemical engineering turns raw materials into chemicals, fuels, medicines and everyday products. Engineers design chemical, gas and pharmaceutical processes, operators run mixers, kilns and production machines, and plant staff control quality and handle hazardous waste safely. Chemical plants, refineries and manufacturing factories are where most of the work happens.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D055", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
