    ('D056', 'start_here', 'Understand Blockchain', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Blockchain work involves building software that records transactions on shared computer networks rather than in one central place. Smart contract and blockchain developers write the programs, security auditors and cryptography engineers test them for weaknesses, and architects and analysts design the wider systems. Software companies and financial organisations offer most roles.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D056", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
