    ('D057', 'start_here', 'Understand Digital Health', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Digital health applies computers and data to the running of healthcare. Clinical coders and records staff manage patient records and coding, analysts study health data, engineers build health information systems and mobile health apps, and managers lead healthcare institutions and informatics teams. Hospitals, clinics, health agencies and technology firms are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D057", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
