    ('D059', 'start_here', 'Understand Space Technology', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Space technology concerns the design and operation of spacecraft and satellites. Aerospace, avionics and satellite systems engineers design and test flight hardware, propulsion engineers work on spacecraft engines, and mission operations engineers run missions once craft are in orbit, drawing heavily on physics. Space agencies, aerospace companies and research organisations are the usual employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D059", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
