    ('D082', 'start_here', 'Understand Customer Service, Contact Centre', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Customer service is the work of helping people by phone, at reception desks and at service counters. Representatives answer calls and handle complaints, receptionists and concierges greet and assist visitors, dispatchers take emergency calls, and medical administrative assistants manage patient records and appointments. Call centres, hotels, hospitals, banks and telecoms companies employ them.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D082", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
