    ('D084', 'start_here', 'Understand Payroll, Bookkeeping', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Payroll and bookkeeping is the careful recording of an organisation''s money, including wages, taxes, sales and payments. Clerks maintain records of financial transactions, prepare staff salaries, process insurance and tax paperwork, and support auditors and back-office operations using office software. Banks, insurance companies and businesses of every size employ them.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D084", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
