    ('D090', 'start_here', 'Understand Animal Care, Grooming', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Animal care and grooming is the everyday looking after of animals, from feeding and cleaning to training and grooming. Attendants and kennel workers care for animals in shelters and boarding facilities, trainers teach dogs and horses, breeders raise animals, and groomers keep coats healthy and tidy. Kennels, stables, zoos and grooming salons are the typical workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D090", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
