    ('D091', 'start_here', 'Understand Driving Instruction', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Driving instruction is the teaching of people to drive safely and pass their licence tests. Instructors give practical lessons in cars, buses, trucks, motorcycles and even vessels, follow a set curriculum, guard each student''s safety and explain the rules of the road. Most work for driving schools accredited by the road safety authorities or run their own.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D091", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
