    ('D094', 'start_here', 'Understand Electronics Servicing, ICT Equipment', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Electronics servicing is the repair and maintenance of electronic devices and communication equipment. Technicians read circuit diagrams to repair phones, computers, alarms and telecoms equipment, install smart-home systems, and test microelectronics and hardware against quality standards. Telecoms companies, repair workshops and manufacturing firms are the typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D094", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
