    ('D097', 'start_here', 'Understand Welding, Fabrication, Blacksmithing', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Welding and fabrication is the shaping and joining of metal into useful products. Welders and solderers fuse metal parts together, operators run plasma cutters and forging presses, and craft workers such as farriers, riveters and gunsmiths make and repair metal items to quality standards. Workshops, factories and construction firms are the usual workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D097", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
