    ('D098', 'start_here', 'Understand Precision Engineering, Toolmaking', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Precision engineering is the making, testing and repair of small, exact components and instruments. Watchmakers and instrument assemblers build and fix watches and optical devices, inspectors test electronics and other products for quality, and toolmakers craft moulds and precision metal parts using measuring equipment. Manufacturing plants, workshops and quality-control laboratories are the typical workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D098", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
