    ('D099', 'start_here', 'Understand Masonry, Bricklaying, Tiling, Plastering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Masonry and its related trades build and finish the solid parts of buildings, such as walls, floors and ceilings. Bricklayers lay blocks, tile fitters and floor layers finish surfaces, ceiling and glass installers fit out interiors, and stone engravers carve decorative work, all under construction safety rules. Most work is with construction firms, and skills can be certified through government trade tests.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D099", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
