    ('D103', 'start_here', 'Understand Jewellery Making, Goldsmithing', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Jewellery making and goldsmithing is the craft of shaping precious metals and stones into rings, chains and other ornaments. Goldsmiths, jewellers, engravers, stone cutters and setters create new pieces, mount and adjust stones, and repair damaged items using specialist equipment. Most practitioners work in small workshops, jewellery shops or craft studios.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D103", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
