    ('D104', 'start_here', 'Understand Pottery, Ceramics, Glass', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Pottery, ceramics and glass covers the craft of forming clay, porcelain and glass into useful and decorative objects. Practitioners such as ceramic painters, glass-blowers, pottery casters, brick moulders and engravers mould, cast, blow, paint and engrave their pieces, often working from their own sketches. They typically work in potteries, glassworks, brickyards and craft studios.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D104", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
