    ('D105', 'start_here', 'Understand Handicraft, Basketry, Textile Craft', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Handicraft, basketry and textile craft is about making goods by hand from fibres, yarn, wicker and similar materials. Weavers, knitters, carpet makers, wicker furniture makers, brush makers, toymakers and artisan papermakers shape these materials using hand techniques and simple equipment they maintain themselves. Work is usually based in small workshops, craft centres and cottage industries.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D105", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
