    ('D106', 'start_here', 'Understand Garment Making, Tailoring, Dressmaking', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Garment making, tailoring and dressmaking turns fabric into clothing and covered furnishings. Dressmakers, sewing machinists, patternmakers and embroiderers cut and sew garments, grade clothing sizes and work to standard sizing systems, while upholsterers cover seats for boats and railway cars. Typical workplaces include tailoring shops, garment factories and fashion houses.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D106", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D106', 'build_next', 'develop and present designs', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Garment Making, Tailoring, Dressmaking work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D106", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
