    ('D107', 'start_here', 'Understand Leather Technology, Shoemaking', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Leather technology and shoemaking covers turning hides into leather and making footwear, bags and other leather goods. Tanners process hides; makers and machine operators cut, stitch, last and finish shoes, including bespoke and orthopaedic footwear; technicians test quality while designers and managers develop products and run production. Employers include tanneries, footwear factories, workshops and leather goods shops.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D107", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
