    ('D109', 'start_here', 'Understand Metal Processing, Foundry', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Metal processing and foundry work is about shaping and finishing metal in industrial plants. Operators run casting, coating, drawing, grinding and abrasive blasting machines, load and remove workpieces, reject faulty ones and keep equipment running to quality standards. They are employed mainly by foundries, steel plants and metal manufacturing factories.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D109", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D109', 'build_next', 'engineering safety and reliability', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Metal Processing, Foundry work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D109", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
