    ('D111', 'start_here', 'Understand Textile, Garment', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Textile and garment manufacturing runs the machinery that spins fibre into yarn and turns yarn into fabric and clothing. Spinning and twisting operators, knitting and finishing technicians and pattern-printing workers run machines, measure yarn, test fabric quality and inspect finished goods, with supervisors managing operations. Textile mills and garment factories are the usual workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D111", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
    ('D111', 'build_next', 'develop and present designs', 'Build this next because the checked domain evidence names it as part of Textile, Garment work and preparation.', 'Named domain-level Nigerian evidence (competency); it is a guidance starting point, not a universal checklist.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 2, '{"source": "nigerian_web_source_evidence", "domain_id": "D111", "evidence_kind": "competency", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
