    ('D112', 'start_here', 'Understand Wood Processing, Pulp', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Wood processing and pulp work converts logs into sawn timber, veneer, pellets, pulp and paper. Machine operators run saws, debarkers, planers, bleachers and paper machines, perform test runs, troubleshoot faults and work safely in protective gear, while supervisors oversee production lines. Sawmills, paper mills and wood products factories are the main employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D112", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
