    ('D114', 'start_here', 'Understand Assembly, Packaging', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Assembly and packaging is the factory work of putting products together and preparing them for sale. Assemblers build motorcycles, aircraft engines, medical devices and electronics by reading assembly drawings and aligning components, while other operators run cartoning, labelling and filling machines. This work happens in factories and assembly plants across many industries.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D114", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
