    ('D115', 'start_here', 'Understand Road Transport Operations (Drivers', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Road transport operations covers moving people and goods by road. Bus, delivery, cargo and refuse vehicle drivers plan routes, obey traffic laws, communicate with customers and understand the basic mechanics of their vehicles. Employers include transport and logistics companies, government agencies and any organisation that runs its own vehicle fleet.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D115", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
