    ('D118', 'start_here', 'Understand Crop Production, Horticulture', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Crop production and horticulture is the growing of food crops, fruit, vegetables and garden plants. Managers and supervisors plan planting, fertilisation and pest control; workers pick produce, apply crop protection and operate vineyard machinery; inspectors check that farms follow agricultural and environmental rules. Farms, plantations, nurseries and agricultural agencies provide most of the work.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D118", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
