    ('D119', 'start_here', 'Understand Livestock, Poultry, Dairy', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Livestock, poultry and dairy work is the rearing of animals for food and other products. Farmers and breeders raise cattle, poultry, sheep, horses and bees and run dairy farms, while livestock workers feed, handle and groom animals under animal-welfare rules. Work is based on farms, ranches and dairies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D119", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
