    ('D121', 'start_here', 'Understand Forestry, Wildlife Management', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Forestry and wildlife management deals with harvesting timber and protecting forests and wild animals. Loggers fell trees, graders inspect lumber, boards and pulp against quality standards, and conservation officers and pest management workers guard forests and wildlife. Forestry companies, sawmills, government agencies and nature reserves offer most positions.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D121", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
