    ('D123', 'start_here', 'Understand Radiography, Medical Imaging', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Radiography and medical imaging uses X-rays, CT, MRI, ultrasound and related technology to see inside the body and to treat disease with radiation. Radiographers and imaging technologists position patients and operate scanners, sonographers perform ultrasound examinations, and radiation therapists deliver radiotherapy. They work mainly in hospitals and diagnostic imaging centres.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D123", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
