    ('D124', 'start_here', 'Understand Community Health Extension', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Community health extension provides frontline basic health care close to where people live. Practitioners give first aid, assist nurses with patient care, collect blood samples, fit spectacles as opticians or optical technicians, sterilise equipment and support patients at home or as hospital porters. Health centres, hospitals and home-care services are the usual workplaces.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D124", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
