    ('D126', 'start_here', 'Understand Complementary, Alternative', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Complementary and alternative medicine treats patients using therapies outside conventional hospital care, such as acupuncture, herbal medicine, homeopathy and aromatherapy. Practitioners including acupuncturists, herbal therapists, chiropractors and naturopaths assess clients, draw on knowledge of human anatomy and physiology, and give hands-on treatments. Many work in private clinics and wellness centres.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D126", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
