    ('D131', 'start_here', 'Understand Motorsport Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Motorsport engineering applies mechanical and production engineering to high-performance vehicles. Powertrain, composites, welding and fluid power engineers design engines, aerodynamics and vehicle systems from technical drawings, while technicians and supervisors test parts and oversee manufacturing. Racing teams, engineering workshops and vehicle manufacturers offer the main opportunities.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D131", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
