    ('D132', 'start_here', 'Understand Space Science, Exploration', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Space science and exploration studies space and builds the craft that travel there. Aerospace and satellite systems engineers design spacecraft, flight and mission controllers monitor missions, and physicists, astrophysicists and astrobiologists carry out research using tools such as spectroscopy. Space agencies, research institutes and universities are the usual employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D132", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
