    ('D134', 'start_here', 'Understand Naval Architecture, Marine Engineering', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Naval architecture and marine engineering is the design of ships and the running of their machinery. Naval architects design and survey vessels and offshore energy installations, while marine engineers operate and maintain ship engines and systems at sea, from assistant to chief engineer. Shipyards, shipping companies and offshore energy firms are typical employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D134", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
