    ('D166', 'start_here', 'Understand Autonomous Vehicles, Self-Driving Systems', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Autonomous vehicle engineering develops cars and other vehicles that can drive themselves. Automotive and powertrain engineers design the vehicle''s mechanical systems, while software, embedded systems and machine learning engineers build the computing that senses the road and controls the car. Vehicle manufacturers, engineering firms and technology companies employ these specialists.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D166", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
