    ('D135', 'start_here', 'Understand Nuclear Engineering, Radiation Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Nuclear engineering and radiation science applies physics to nuclear energy and radiation. Nuclear engineers and reactor operators run and decommission reactors, health and medical physicists keep people safe from radiation and support radiotherapy, and radiochemists work in laboratories using mathematical modelling and spectroscopy. Power stations, hospitals, research institutes and regulators employ them.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D135", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
