    ('D144', 'start_here', 'Understand Climate Science, Meteorology', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Climate science and meteorology study the weather and the long-term behaviour of the atmosphere. Forecasters and meteorologists use instruments and specialised computer models to predict weather conditions, while climatologists, hydrologists and oceanographers analyse climate, water and ocean patterns. Typical employers are government weather agencies, aviation organisations and research institutes.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D144", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
