    ('D145', 'start_here', 'Understand Neuroscience, Cognitive Science', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Neuroscience and cognitive science investigate the brain, thought and behaviour. One side of the field involves scientists studying how the brain and mind work; the other involves psychologists and psychotherapists who assess and treat mental and behavioural health. They work in hospitals, clinics, schools and universities.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D145", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
