    ('D155', 'start_here', 'Understand Nanotechnology, Advanced Materials', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Nanotechnology and advanced materials involve studying and building substances at extremely small scales to give them new properties. Chemists, materials scientists and nanofabrication technicians run experiments, analyse chemical substances, make tiny components and write up their findings in technical papers. Research laboratories, universities and manufacturing companies are the usual employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D155", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
