    ('D141', 'start_here', 'Understand Quantum Computing, Quantum Information', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Quantum computing builds a new kind of computer based on the physics of atoms and light. Some specialists write quantum software, algorithms and cryptography, while others engineer the hardware, sensors and devices that run them. Work in this field is usually found in research laboratories, universities and technology companies.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D141", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
