    ('D167', 'start_here', 'Understand XR & Immersive Technology', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Immersive technology, often called XR, creates virtual and augmented reality experiences that blend digital content with the real world. Developers code AR, VR and spatial computing applications, while hardware engineers design headsets, optics, haptics and motion capture systems. Technology companies, studios and research laboratories are where most of this work happens.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D167", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
