    ('D070', 'start_here', 'Understand Performing Arts & Entertainment', 'Start here because the domain definition explains the field before a student chooses a specialised area or role.', 'Domain definition: Performing arts and entertainment covers live and recorded performance, including acting, music, dance and stage production. Performers such as dancers, musicians, conductors and presenters create the show itself, while technical crews run lighting, sound, props, costumes and stage machinery behind the scenes. Theatres, studios, broadcasters and event companies are the usual employers.', 'https://esco.ec.europa.eu/en/use-esco', 1, '{"source": "domain_definition_library_and_domain_meta", "domain_id": "D070", "guidance_layer": "global_domain_foundation_v1", "ownership": "domain_owned"}'),
